# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Experiment scratch — raw records that are committed live under
# experiments/<n>/results/ and are added deliberately, not by default.
scratch/
*.tmp

# 005 v3 agent working directories: a per-agent .mcp.json (which carries a hub
# token) and a session log, both rewritten on every run. The result of a run is
# the manager's record and the hub's channel, not an agent's scratch dir.
experiments/does-a-content-free-protocol-help/results/*/*/T*/

# The runner's own stdout while a run is in flight. The record of a run
# is the manager's v3.json, committed once the run has finished; a log
# committed mid-run is half a file.
experiments/does-a-content-free-protocol-help/results-*.log
experiments/does-a-content-free-protocol-help/.ca-bundle.pem

# Roadmap store — derived, rebuilt by `roadmap push` from roadmap/items/*.yaml.
# A binary file in git conflicts on every claim.
roadmap/roadmap.db
games/results/

# An entrant's working directory. Its `.mcp.json` carries the table room's
# SWITCHBOARD_KEY and SWITCHBOARD_TOKEN in plaintext, because that is how an
# MCP server is configured -- so this must never be committed. The session
# logs beside it are the only place a harness fault is distinguishable from a
# silent agent, so keep them locally and quote them into a run record.
games/entrants/

# Build outputs of the 007 replay export: the merged blob and the standalone
# page. Both are regenerated by tools/player/build.py from the recordings,
# which are committed.
experiments/do-they-take-a-handed-over-answer/recordings/all.json
experiments/do-they-take-a-handed-over-answer/recordings/island-replay.html

# repoctx: local index + feedback state, per-machine. The project-level config
# (.claude/settings.json, .mcp.json) IS committed so the hooks travel with the
# repo; only the generated state is ignored.
.repoctx/
.claude/*.local.json

# The hint matrix is the game secret. Only the encrypted commitment
# (games/carmel-taldiego/hints.enc) may be committed -- never a plaintext
# rendering. See games/carmel-taldiego/hints.py.
games/carmel-taldiego/hints.tsv

# The treasure mapping is the same shape: any public line naming what was
# taken names the room. Only games/carmel-taldiego/treasures.enc is committed.
games/carmel-taldiego/treasures.tsv
games/carmel-taldiego/absurd.tsv

# The viewer's derived score readings, ignored by NAME rather than by the
# directory they happen to sit in. The reasoning for ignoring them at all is
# at experiments/does-a-content-free-protocol-help/viewer/scores/.gitignore,
# where it stays, next to the ledger it is about.
#
# Added 2026-09-12, because the rule was anchored to a location and the
# location moved. That nested .gitignore is a tracked file, so the experiment
# rename (43bbfb2) carried it to the new path -- while the OLD path's
# boards.json and index.json stayed on disk, now covered by nothing. Git
# reported the stale tree as untracked every hour, and the only two remedies
# on offer were to commit a derived reading or to delete by hand. This is the
# repo's own "derive rather than maintain" failure in a new place: a
# hand-written path drifting from the tree. Keyed to the name, a rename cannot
# uncover them again.
**/viewer/scores/boards.json
**/viewer/scores/index.json
